1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,710
It was a regular Saturday morning, just like any other.
那是一个普通的周六早上，和平常没什么两样。

2
00:00:05,510 --> 00:00:09,570
I was driving my nine-year-old daughter, Emma, to her weekly swimming lesson.
我正开车送九岁的女儿埃玛去上每周一次的游泳课。

3
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:15,630
Recently, Emma had started seeing me as a true hero who could solve any problem fairly.
最近，埃玛开始把我看作一位真正的英雄，觉得我能公正地解决任何问题。

4
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:19,170
“You always know what’s right, Dad,” she would say.
“爸爸，你总是知道怎么做才对。”她常这样说。

5
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:24,340
We were talking about her class when I noticed a crowd up ahead and had to slow down.
我们正聊着她班上的事，我注意到前方聚着一群人，只好放慢车速。

6
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:28,070
People were gathered on the street, pointing and laughing.
人们聚在街上，指指点点，哈哈大笑。

7
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:31,700
In the middle of it all was a large brown and white cow.
人群正中是一头棕白相间的大母牛。

8
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,610
It looked completely lost and terrified.
它看上去完全迷失了方向，惊恐万分。

9
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:39,460
Some kids were shouting nearby, which seemed to scare the animal even more.
附近有些孩子在大喊大叫，这似乎让那头牲畜更害怕了。

10
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,540
A strong feeling of anger rose inside me.
一股强烈的怒火在我心中升起。

11
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:46,520
These people were treating the poor creature’s fear as entertainment.
这些人把这可怜的动物的恐惧当成了消遣。

12
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:50,520
“Dad, that cow is scared,” Emma said softly from the back seat.
“爸爸，那头牛害怕了。”埃玛在后座轻声说。

13
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:52,210
“What would you do?”
“你会怎么做？”

14
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:54,360
Her question was serious.
她问得很认真。

15
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,990
She believed I would do the right thing.
她相信我会做正确的事。

16
00:00:57,790 --> 00:01:03,560
“Well,” I said, trying to sound confident for her, “I would calm it down and help it find its way home.”
“嗯，”为了在她面前显得有把握，我说道，“我会让它平静下来，帮它找到回家的路。”

17
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:06,450
I explained that I knew a lot about cows.
我解释说，我对牛很在行。

18
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:11,970
I spent my childhood on a farm, and now I even worked at a beef processing plant.
我的童年是在农场度过的，如今甚至还在一家牛肉加工厂工作。

19
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:14,990
I was sure my experience would impress Emma.
我确信我的经历会让埃玛刮目相看。

20
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:19,530
After dropping off a very impressed Emma, I turned my car around.
把对我佩服不已的埃玛送下车后，我掉转了车头。

21
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:22,560
I felt it was my duty to go back and help.
我觉得回去帮忙是我的责任。

22
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:25,660
When I returned, the scene was worse.
等我回来时，场面更糟了。

23
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:33,530
I learned from a shop owner that the cow had been wandering for a while, knocking over a fruit stand and causing quite a bit of trouble.
我从一个店主那里得知，那头牛已经游荡了一阵子，撞翻了一个水果摊，惹了不少麻烦。

24
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:38,700
I took a slow, careful step towards the animal, speaking in a gentle voice.
我小心翼翼地朝那头牲畜慢慢迈出一步，用温和的声音跟它说话。

25
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:44,490
However, instead of calming down, the cow lowered its head and let out a threatening sound.
然而，那头牛非但没有平静下来，反而低下头，发出一声带着威胁的叫声。

26
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:48,180
It stared directly at me, full of hostility.
它直勾勾地瞪着我，满是敌意。

27
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:52,070
My confidence faded, replaced by a sudden fear.
我的信心消失了，取而代之的是突如其来的恐惧。

28
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:54,590
This wasn’t going to be easy at all.
这事可一点也不容易。

29
00:01:55,390 --> 00:01:59,800
Just as I was about to turn and run, two police officers arrived on the scene.
就在我准备转身逃跑时，两名警察赶到了现场。

30
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:05,390
After we managed to secure the cow to a tree, we began to discuss what to do with it.
我们设法把牛拴在一棵树上之后，开始商量怎么处置它。
